/-!
# Two-species fresh-copy spectral readout

`twoSpeciesQPEProgram` uses fresh copies of two density operators to approximate controlled
evolution generated by their difference. The module compares actual and ideal circuit execution
and derives the ideal label law for an arbitrary density-operator input `χ` in a unitary
eigenbasis of `ρ - σ`.

The event bounds and exact copy ledger make this readout available to the state-discrimination
application of quantum principal component analysis in [LloydMohseniRebentrost2014].

## Main statements

* `two_species_qpe_actual_program_state_error`: proves output normalization and a trace-norm
  error bound.
* `twoSpeciesQPEIdealOutput_spectral_label`: expresses ideal labels as an input-weighted
  spectral kernel mixture.
* `two_species_qpe_actual_spectral_label_event_refined`: bounds event error and records the
  exact two-species resources.

## References

* [Lloyd et al., 2014][LloydMohseniRebentrost2014]
-/

